estion." :question/worked-solution "First, we have to find $a+b$. The given directions are perpendicular, so the triangle law of addition gives a right triangle.\n\nTo find the unit vector corresponding to $a+b$, we have to divide by the magnitude:\n\n$$\nu=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\n$$\n\nTo find the magnitude, we can use the Pythagorean theorem:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|a+b|^2&=|a|^2+|b|^2\\\\\n&=10^2+13^2\\\\\n&=100+169\\\\\n&=269\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the magnitude is\n\n$$\n|a+b|=\\sqrt{269}=\\sqrt{269}\n$$\n\nand the corresponding unit vector is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u&=\\frac{a+b}{|a+b|}\\\\\n&=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{269}}(a+b)\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502475 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5187951d-7851-587d-950c-40bb153d472f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502469} {:answer/id #uuid "6e2a4a21-5bb0-58a1-947a-94a1e48e9040" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{31}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502477} {:answer/id #uuid "8db1a6cd-dc5f-5a94-827b-105391468bba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{24}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502491} {:answer/id #uuid "b2829203-bf6a-5c53-a2c3-4e8f9c2d513b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{625}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502505} {:answer/id #uuid "d27c1ed4-497a-5760-94ef-c9d5868e78f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{7}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502514}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "5187951d-7851-587d-950c-40bb153d472f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{25}(a + b)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502469} :answer-field/id #uuid "2aef0246-9ad6-53c6-bd16-842273614654" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502445}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question